# cases the riscv32 column cannot build: a case name per line, then the reason.
# entries are written out by name rather than globbed by family, so a case added
# later inherits nothing and has to be reviewed against this file on its way in.
#
# two kinds of entry live here. a TARGET LIMITATION names a construct the target
# refuses by design. a MACH DEFECT names one rv32imafdc can express and the
# compiler refuses the o2 build for (#3617); each is deleted by the change that
# closes it. the run fails on a listed case that builds, so a line cannot go stale.

# ---- TARGET LIMITATION ----

ct/mul_secret        a secret multiply is refused: rv32imafdc does not select Zkt, which every RISC-V data-independent multiply row names. riscv64zkt-linux carries the case.
ct/mul_secret128     same refusal, and the case's 128-bit product type is not realized on riscv32 either (#3511).
int128/arith_u128    "a 128-bit integer is not realized on riscv32: the target declares no integer of that width". rv32 declares integers of 1, 2, 4 and 8 bytes only; a 128-bit value would be four lanes, which the lane plan does not model (#3511, ruling Q7).
